==English==
{{was wotd|2006|April|28}}

===Etymology===
Generally considered to derive from {{etyl|nl|en}}, although a specific etymon is unclear. ''Century'' and some other old dictionaries derive it from a confusion of two similar {{etyl|nl|en}} words, namely {{m|nl|*mallemerok||foolish woman}} (from {{m|nl|mal|malle|foolish}} + {{m|nl|*marok}}, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|marotte||jester's sceptre}}) and {{m|nl|*mallemok||sailor of a whaling vessel}}, but the first of those words is not attested<!--or does not seem to be...-->, and the second is not attested with the claimed meaning (but see {{m|en|mollymawk}}). Compare {{m|nl|mallemolen}}.

